    fix(selftest): reject non-object, duplicate-id, bad-status board rows — Addresses CF-088.
    
    Validate the real board and fixture boards through the same single-process
    board arm. Report every offending line, duplicate id and first occurrence,
    and invalid or missing status. Preserve newline-terminated record counting
    and fail closed with a named reason when python3 is unavailable.
    
    Section 7b exercises null, array, string, number, missing id, duplicate id,
    bad status, missing status and malformed JSON fixtures. Exact pre-fix arm
    controls accepted the same eight syntactically valid fixture files (3/3)
    that the new arm rejects (2 of 3). The real board passes 85/85 rows.
    
    Verified: bash -n tests/selftest.sh; bash tests/selftest.sh (SELFTEST: PASS);
    scripts/boardctl validate (RESULT: OK, 28 existing warnings).
    No board changes; no push. The final trace names the identical-tree content
    commit before this message is amended, avoiding a self-referential hash.
    
